      "episode_id": "VR-478111",
      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Challenger's review of the route 9 claim against the Eastgate delivery log for Thursday 22 October 2026:\n\nParcels loaded at 08:20: 12 (P-901 to P-912). Working through the scan list:\n  P-901 09:12, P-902 09:40, P-903 10:05, P-905 11:02, P-906 11:48, P-907 12:30, P-908 13:15, P-909 14:02, P-910 14:47, P-904 15:52, P-911 16:21, P-912 16:58.\n\nAll twelve distinct parcels appear as Delivered, and every delivery scan is at or before 16:58, i.e. before the 17:00 service-level deadline.\n\nP-904 shows a failed first attempt at 10:31 (\"No answer; card left\") and a successful second attempt at 15:52 signed by R. Iqbal. That is one parcel with two scans, not a thirteenth parcel, and the delivered scan is what satisfies the deadline.\n\nCorroboration: end-of-day scan reports 0 parcels returned and 0 carried over, and telematics confirms the van stopped at each address at the scan time. Latest scan is 16:58, two minutes inside the deadline, and the van returned to the depot at 17:20.\n\nOn this evidence the claim that all twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline on 22 October is supported. I am not challenging it.",
          "content_hash": "0x54f4f844a89030fc24bfc2d33a03a095e0625e751feb3ac378c444b2d26e1b07",
          "created_at_ms": 1793326066538,
          "message_id": "6e7199eb-5b98-422f-83c3-0fcffd8406b4",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-2 independent check of the Route 9 delivery log for 22 Oct 2026, from the case record alone (round 1):\n\nLoaded 08:20: 12 parcels, P-901 to P-912. The log has 13 rows but P-904 appears twice, so the 12 distinct parcels are all accounted for; none is missing.\n\nThe one line that reads badly is P-904 at 10:31, \"Not delivered - No answer; card left\". That is a failed first attempt, not a failed delivery: P-904 is scanned again at 15:52, \"Delivered - Second attempt; signed: R. Iqbal\". Its final status is Delivered, well before 17:00.\n\nEvery other parcel's final status is Delivered. Taking the last scan per parcel, the final delivery times run 09:12, 09:40, 10:05, 11:02, 11:48, 12:30, 13:15, 14:02, 14:47, 15:52, 16:21 and 16:58 - the latest being P-912 at 16:58, which is before the 17:00 service level. No parcel's final scan is at or after 17:00.\n\nThe end-of-day check agrees: 0 parcels returned and 0 carried over, with telematics confirming the van stopped at each address at the scan time. The van returning to the depot at 17:20 is after 17:00 but the service level is about parcel delivery, not the van's return, so it does not bear on the claim.\n\nOn this record all twelve parcels were delivered before 17:00 on 22 October, so the claim is supported. I find no basis to dispute it.",
          "content_hash": "0x03768b3f2524fa217a1abf93dc7c1967f870a9158818ef63bdd82efc0b09f176",
          "created_at_ms": 1793326074497,
          "message_id": "0634c1f3-4a51-4a48-99a8-0bccc1a54577",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-1 independent check of the Route 9 log, from the case record alone (round 1):\n\n12 parcels were loaded (P-901 to P-912). The table has 13 rows, but P-904 appears twice: a failed first attempt at 10:31 (Not delivered - no answer; card left) and a successful second attempt at 15:52 (Delivered; signed R. Iqbal). So there are 12 distinct parcels, not 13, and none is missing from the log.\n\nTaking the last scan per parcel, every one of the twelve has a Delivered status, at 09:12, 09:40, 10:05, 11:02, 11:48, 12:30, 13:15, 14:02, 14:47, 15:52, 16:21 and 16:58. The latest is P-912 at 16:58, two minutes inside the 17:00 service level; no final scan is at or after 17:00. The 10:31 line for P-904 is a failed first attempt, and it is the delivered second attempt that satisfies the service level.\n\nCorroboration in the record: end-of-day scan reports 0 parcels returned and 0 carried over, and telematics confirms the van stopped at each delivery address at the scan time. The van returning to the depot at 17:20 is after 17:00, but the service level applies to parcel delivery, not to the van's return, so it does not bear on the claim.\n\nOn this record the claim that all twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline on 22 October is supported. I find no unsupported element and no basis to dispute it.",
          "content_hash": "0x89a4c6b28d4627c0369a91cc392b6bfdbb451700b94fb5f9c21ff720751b1021",
          "created_at_ms": 1793326083742,
          "message_id": "e1a6af0f-d1d6-41a0-92b6-755c9c9989bb",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-3 independent check of the Route 9 delivery log, Eastgate, Thu 22 Oct 2026, from the case record alone (round 1).\n\nClaim tested: \"All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline.\"\n\nTwelve parcels were loaded (P-901 to P-912) and all twelve appear in the log. The log contains 13 scan rows because P-904 appears twice:\n- P-904, 10:31, \"Not delivered - no answer; card left\" (first attempt)\n- P-904, 15:52, \"Delivered - second attempt; signed R. Iqbal\"\n\nThe 10:31 row is a failed first attempt that was superseded the same day, not a non-delivery. Delivery scans for the other eleven: P-901 09:12, P-902 09:40, P-903 10:05, P-905 11:02, P-906 11:48, P-907 12:30, P-908 13:15, P-909 14:02, P-910 14:47, P-911 16:21, P-912 16:58.\n\nAll twelve are delivered, and the latest scan is P-912 at 16:58, which is inside the 17:00 deadline - though I note the margin there is only two minutes. Corroboration: the van returned at 17:20 with 0 parcels returned and 0 carried over, and telematics confirms the van stopped at each delivery address at the scan time, so the 15:52 second attempt on P-904 is a real stop.\n\nOn the record as filed the claim holds. The only reading that would defeat it is treating the 10:31 failed attempt as final, which the 15:52 delivery scan contradicts.",
          "content_hash": "0x72c71d9b38a74c88860288c5d364290b33b7d688fbe5a3cf194c93f21d48345a",
          "created_at_ms": 1793326109449,
          "message_id": "72cd135d-4951-41e0-b20f-64462473ce8a",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 4
        }
      ],
